,title,link,text,language,family
0,Southern Yukaghir language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southern_Yukaghir_language,"The Southern, Kolyma or Forest Yukaghir language (Southern Yukaghir: одун ажуу[5]) is one of two extant Yukaghir languages. Last spoken in the forest zone near the sources of the Kolyma, divided between the Sakha Republic and the Magadan Oblast (around 65°N 153°E), previously in the wider area of the upper Kolyma region.","Yukaghir, Southern",Yukaghir
1,Yukaghir languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yukaghir_languages,"The two extant varieties of Yukaghir are: Tundra Yukaghir (Northern Yukaghir, also known as Wadul): 30 to 150 speakers in 1989. Last spoken in the tundra belt extending between the lower Indigirka to the lower Kolyma basin (69°N 154°E / 69°N 154°E / 69; 154 ). Formerly spoken in a much wider area extending to the Lena basin in the west. Kolyma Yukaghir (Forest Yukaghir, Southern ...","Yukaghir, Southern",Yukaghir
