6,The History of The Study of Yukaghir Musical Culture,https://ling.tspu.ru/en/archive.html?year=2019&issue=4&article_id=7689,"Choreographer M. Ya. Zhornitskaya describing circular and imitative dances based on the field materials collected in 1959 and 1964. Yukaghir music became an object of research from 1960s, when composers and musicologists G. A. Grigoryan, E. Ye. Alekseev, G. N. Komrakov began to record examples of musical folklore and study them.","Yukaghir, Southern",Yukaghir
7,Yukaghir languages | 音楽と多言語,https://multilingualwmusic.wixsite.com/home/en/language-family/yukaghir,Yukaghir languagesの分類。またYukaghir languagesの言語で歌われている音楽(洋楽)のYouTube動画を掲載しています。,"Yukaghir, Southern",Yukaghir
8,Online Kolyma Yukaghir Documentation - sgr.fi,https://www.sgr.fi/yukaghir/intro/yukaghirs.html,"Several centuries ago there used to be several Yukaghir idioms, but by the time the systematic study of Yukaghir began at the end of 19th century only two varieties had survived. They are usually referred to as Kolyma (or Southern) and Tundra (or Northern) Yukaghir and are spoken by the Kolyma and Tundra Yukaghirs, respectively. The distances between the habitats of these two groups is large ...","Yukaghir, Southern",Yukaghir
